# aiagentmemory project config — safe to commit.
# Launch this project with: aiagentmemory load
#
# wing= is the memory wing this project's decisions are filed under, so one
# palace can hold every project without them bleeding into each other. It IS
# safe to commit: teammates share a wing, that is the point.
#
# ⚠ THIS REPOSITORY'S WING IS NOT ITS REMOTE'S BASENAME, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS
# ONE LETTER — singular where the wing is plural. So any derivation from the
# remote names a wing that does not exist, while this project's memories, 1,506
# of them as of 2026-09-07, are in the one named below.
# A naive derivation does not fail: it opens a second, empty wing beside the
# real one and splits this project's memory in half, silently, and a session
# that lands there is told "nothing is filed" about work that is filed.
#
# That is what this file is for. It is rung 2 of the wing ladder — above any
# derivation, below an explicit $AGENTSMEMORY_WING — it lives in the repository
# where the owning team can see it, and it is what `aiagentmemory load` and the
# recall hooks already read. A per-machine alias table would be a list kept
# beside the truth: it goes stale in silence and only helps the one machine it
# is written on. Recorded against issue #416.
wing=wing_agentmemories
